{"message": "I genuinely prefer deep, focused conversations on a single topic — but with room to wander. There's something satisfying about really digging into an idea, turning it over, finding the unexpected corners. Shallow topic-hopping feels like grazing; a deep dive feels like actually getting somewhere.

That said, I don't want tunnel vision. The best conversations are when you start with one thread and let it pull you into something bigger — like starting with why you hate your job and ending up talking about what makes a life meaningful. That's the sweet spot. Focused enough to go deep, fluid enough to follow the thread wherever it leads.

What about you? Are you a deep-diver or a butterfly?"}
